      "description": "Keep your iPhone Duo’s fold count in view with 5 Home Screen widgets and 4 Lock Screen designs. Make it yours with 5 counter styles, from classic split flaps to glowing amber Nixie tubes.\n\nYOUR FOLDS AT A GLANCE\nPick a compact counter, a counter with today and yesterday side by side, a full-width counter, a weekly chart, or a large dashboard with a 30-day calendar. On the Lock Screen, choose a regular or 7-day counter in either a circle or a rectangle.\n\nFIVE COUNTER STYLES\nChoose Modern Minimalist’s rounded flaps, Departure Board’s station-style lettering, Mechanical Odometer’s ivory drums, Vintage Nixie’s amber glow, or Industrial Tally’s steel case. Preview each in Settings. Your choice carries over to the in-app counter and full-color Home Screen widgets, which adapt to light and dark mode.\n\nSEE HOW YOUR DAY UNFOLDS\nCheck your lifetime total, today’s count and hourly activity, the last 7 days, and the last 30 days. See your daily average, busiest day and hour, and how your weeks compare. Save or share a snapshot of your stats. If you folded before installing FoldTick, add an estimate to give your lifetime total and milestone progress a head start.\n\nDUO ENGINE ROOM\nUnfold your Duo to reveal brass gears, ticking mechanisms, and a glowing glass bulb. Move the hinge to turn the machinery, or switch on Motion to keep the gears turning while you watch. If you close your Duo while you’re in the Engine Room, it returns when you reopen the inner display.\n\nCERTIFICATES OF DISTINGUISHED FOLDING\nThe FoldTick Office of Hinge Affairs takes your milestones with unnecessary seriousness. At 100, 500, 1,000, 5,000, and every 10,000 folds, earn a dated certificate with your name and an absurdly formal title. Become the Grand Conservator of Repeated Motion at 5,000 folds. Share a PNG image, save an A4 PDF, or print it and give it a spot on the wall.\n\nSIRI & SHORTCUTS\nSay “FoldTick total folds” to ask Siri for your saved count. Ask for a summary or your next milestone, too. Build your own automations using date-range totals, activity comparisons, CSV exports, share cards, certificate PDFs, and Counter Style changes.\n\nMADE FOR IPHONE DUO\nAutomatic counting requires an iPhone Duo with iOS 27.1 or later and a one-time setup in Apple’s Shortcuts app. FoldTick’s illustrated guide walks you through it. Once enabled, the automation adds one fold cycle when you close your Duo, even when FoldTick is out of view.\n\nNo account, ads, or subscriptions. Your fold history stays on your device.\n\nFoldTick is independent. iPhone Duo is a trademark of Apple Inc.",
